# serializer version: 1
# name: test_audit_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools audit COMMAND
  
  Report what a proof's sources ask a verifier to accept
  
  ╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ trust  Audit Rust sources for items the verifier was told to accept.         │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_audit_trust_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools audit trust [OPTIONS] PATHS
  
  Audit Rust sources for items the verifier was told to accept.
  
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ *  PATHS --paths --empty-paths  Rust files to start from [required]          │
  │    --repo-root --root PATH      Repository root that bounds the audit and    │
  │                                 anchors every reported                       │
  │                                 location. Defaults to the current working    │
  │                                 directory. [env var: INPUT_REPO_ROOT]        │
  │    --procedural-macro           Scan string literals as well as code, for a  │
  │      --no-procedural-macro      proc-macro crate that can                    │
  │                                 turn them into code.  By default the crate   │
  │                                 kind is read from the nearest                │
  │                                 `Cargo.toml` above each source; either flag  │
  │                                 states it for every source                   │
  │                                 instead. [env var: INPUT_PROCEDURAL_MACRO]   │
  │    --prover STR...              Provers whose vocabularies to apply, named   │
  │                                 `kani` or `verus`. This                      │
  │                                 option may be repeated; without it both      │
  │                                 vocabularies are applied.                    │
  │    --format CHOICE              Output form, defaulting to text. [choices:   │
  │                                 text, json] [default: text]                  │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_analyse_log_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani analyse-log --log PATH --manifest PATH [OPTIONS]
  
  Analyse a captured Kani log against a harness manifest.
  
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ *  --log PATH                   Complete captured output of one Kani         │
  │                                 invocation. [required]                       │
  │ *  --manifest PATH              Harness manifest declaring claims, controls  │
  │                                 and covers. [required]                       │
  │    --harness STR...             Harness names to select from the manifest;   │
  │                                 defaults to all of them.                     │
  │    --require-full-profile       Whether to fail unless the run covered the   │
  │      --no-require-full-profile  whole selected manifest with                 │
  │                                 unwinding checks enabled. [default: False]   │
  │    --format CHOICE              Output form, defaulting to text. [choices:   │
  │                                 text, json] [default: text]                  │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_exec_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani exec --installation STR --cwd STR --extra-arg STR...
  
  Execute an already installed, qualified Kani 0.67 Linux release.
  
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ *  --installation STR   Literal release-root path text, containing bin and   │
  │                         toolchain directories. [env var: INPUT_INSTALLATION] │
  │                         [required]                                           │
  │ *  --cwd STR            Literal proof-directory path text; relative paths    │
  │                         use the process cwd. [env var: INPUT_CWD] [required] │
  │ *  --extra-arg STR...   Literal verifier arguments, provided with repeated   │
  │      --empty-extra-arg  --extra-arg options. [env var: INPUT_EXTRA_ARG]      │
  │                         [required]                                           │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_harnesses_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani harnesses COMMAND
  
  Inspect and run Kani harnesses under supervision
  
  ╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ list  Print the resolved, package-qualified harness inventory as JSON.       │
  │ run   Run every selected harness under supervision.                          │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_harnesses_list_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani harnesses list [OPTIONS]
  
  Print the resolved, package-qualified harness inventory as JSON.
  
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --repo-root PATH   Repository or workspace root. Defaults to the current     │
  │                    directory.                                                │
  │ --package STR...   Packages to discover, repeatable. Empty selects every     │
  │   --empty-package  package.                                                  │
  │ --inventory PATH   Authoritative version-1 inventory document, overriding    │
  │                    discovery.                                                │
  │ --output PATH      Write the JSON here instead of standard output.           │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_harnesses_run_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani harnesses run [OPTIONS]
  
  Run every selected harness under supervision.
  
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --repo-root PATH           Repository or workspace root. Defaults to the     │
  │                            current directory.                                │
  │ --package STR...           Packages to discover, repeatable.                 │
  │   --empty-package                                                            │
  │ --harness STR...           Harness pretty names to run, repeatable.          │
  │   --empty-harness                                                            │
  │ --inventory PATH           Authoritative version-1 inventory document.       │
  │ --installation PATH        Qualified Kani release root, for the legacy       │
  │                            route.                                            │
  │ --cwd PATH                 Proof working directory; required with            │
  │                            `installation`.                                   │
  │ --snapshot-pin PATH        Reviewed snapshot pin, for the snapshot route.    │
  │ --cache-dir PATH           Snapshot cache root.                              │
  │ --extra-arg STR...         Additional verifier arguments, preserved          │
  │   --empty-extra-arg        verbatim.                                         │
  │ --timeout-seconds FLOAT    Wall-clock budget per harness. [default: 1200.0]  │
  │ --sample-interval-seconds  Resource sampling interval. [default: 5.0]        │
  │   FLOAT                                                                      │
  │ --heartbeat-seconds FLOAT  Heartbeat interval while the prover is silent.    │
  │                            [default: 15.0]                                   │
  │ --watchdog --no-watchdog   Stop a harness when host available memory falls   │
  │                            below the floor. [default: True]                  │
  │ --watchdog-mib INT         Available-memory floor in MiB. [default: 1024]    │
  │ --human PATH               Append the human job log here instead of standard │
  │                            output.                                           │
  │ --jsonl PATH               Append versioned JSONL evidence here.             │
  │ --report PATH              Write the final JSON report here.                 │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani COMMAND
  
  Manage Kani verifier installation and version checking
  
  ╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ analyse-log    Analyse a captured Kani log against a harness manifest.       │
  │ check-version  Check that the installed Kani version matches the pin.        │
  │ exec           Execute an already installed, qualified Kani 0.67 Linux       │
  │                release.                                                      │
  │ harnesses      Inspect and run Kani harnesses under supervision              │
  │ install        Install the pinned Kani verifier.                             │
  │ run            Run a proof through the exact installed snapshot. Place --    │
  │                before verifier arguments.                                    │
  │ snapshot       Install and check one immutable Kani snapshot                 │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_install_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani install [OPTIONS]
  
  Install the pinned Kani verifier.
  
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --repo-root PATH        Repository root used to resolve default tool pin     │
  │                         paths. [env var: INPUT_REPO_ROOT, INPUT_REPO_ROOT]   │
  │ --version-file PATH     Optional Kani version pin override. [env var:        │
  │                         INPUT_VERSION_FILE, INPUT_KANI_VERSION_FILE,         │
  │                         INPUT_VERSION_FILE]                                  │
  │ --version STR           Optional semantic version override. [env var:        │
  │                         INPUT_VERSION, INPUT_VERSION]                        │
  │ --setup --no-setup      Whether to run `cargo kani setup` after              │
  │                         installation. [env var: INPUT_SETUP] [default: True] │
  │ --verify --no-verify    Whether to run `cargo kani --version` after          │
  │                         installation. [env var: INPUT_VERIFY] [default:      │
  │                         True]                                                │
  │ --compile --no-compile  Whether to compile Kani from source instead of       │
  │                         installing the pinned                                │
  │                         prebuilt release. [env var: INPUT_KANI_COMPILE,      │
  │                         INPUT_COMPILE] [default: False]                      │
  │ --install-dir PATH      Directory for prebuilt Kani executables. Defaults to │
  │                         Cargo's binary                                       │
  │                         directory. [env var: KANI_INSTALL_DIR,               │
  │                         INPUT_KANI_INSTALL_DIR, INPUT_INSTALL_DIR]           │
  │ --cache-dir PATH        Directory for verified Kani archives. Defaults to    │
  │                         `.cache/kani` below                                  │
  │                         the repository root. [env var: KANI_CACHE_DIR,       │
  │                         INPUT_KANI_CACHE_DIR, INPUT_CACHE_DIR]               │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_run_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani run --snapshot-pin PATH [OPTIONS] [ARGS...]
  
  Run a proof through the exact installed snapshot. Place -- before verifier 
  arguments.
  
  ╭─ Arguments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ ARGS                                                                         │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ *  --snapshot-pin PATH  Required reviewed pin for this proof. [required]     │
  │    --repo-root PATH     Repository root; also the proof working directory.   │
  │    --cache-dir PATH     Snapshot cache. Defaults to `.kani-snapshots`.       │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_snapshot_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani snapshot COMMAND
  
  Install and check one immutable Kani snapshot
  
  ╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ check    Check that the active generation still matches its reviewed pin.    │
  │ install  Install a reviewed snapshot from a local verified asset directory.  │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_kani_snapshot_install_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools kani snapshot install [OPTIONS]
  
  Install a reviewed snapshot from a local verified asset directory.
  
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ --pin PATH        Reviewed pin. Defaults to `tools/kani/snapshot.toml`.      │
  │ --repo-root PATH  Repository root used for default paths.                    │
  │ --cache-dir PATH  Snapshot cache. Defaults to `.kani-snapshots`.             │
  │ --asset-dir PATH  Directory holding the release files and their attestation  │
  │                   bundle.                                                    │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
