# name: test_verus_analyse_log_help_snapshot
  '''
  Usage: prover-tools verus analyse-log --log PATH [OPTIONS]
  
  Analyse a captured Verus log.
  
  ╭─ Parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
  │ *  --log PATH            Complete captured output of one Verus invocation,   │
  │                          with both streams. [required]                       │
  │    --expect-failure STR  ``path[:start[-end]]`` where a negative-control run │
  │                          was required to                                     │
  │                          fail.  Exactly one located failure must land inside │
  │                          it.                                                 │
  │    --require-full        Whether to fail unless the run verified the whole   │
  │      --no-require-full   crate rather than a                                 │
  │                          selection made with ``--verify-*``. [default:       │
  │                          False]                                              │
  │    --verus-release STR   The Verus release the log was captured from.        │
  │                          Defaults to the consumer's                          │
  │                          ``tools/verus/VERSION`` pin when one exists;        │
  │                          without either, the                                 │
  │                          release is left unnamed rather than guessed.        │
  │    --repo-root PATH      Repository root holding the pin.  Defaults to the   │
  │                          working directory.                                  │
  │    --format CHOICE       Output form, defaulting to text. [choices: text,    │
  │                          json] [default: text]                               │
  ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
  
  '''
# ---
